#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:5
#: 897af3426b6c4c5aa4603d7f28a7a8f1
msgid "Adding a new Log Message"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:7
#: edb687b858d245dd90fefdf5e64fdeb7
msgid ":ref:`DataFlash Logs <common-logs>` are stored on the flight controller's onboard dataflash memory and can be downloaded after a flight.  The logs provide detailed information about each flight which can be important especially when trying to :ref:`diagnose why something went wrong <common-diagnosing-problems-using-logs>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:12
#: a11a178cf55d41a381c97bfb38836a53
msgid "This page explains how to write a new dataflash log message."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:14
#: 34f8e1915f5441438a8e7b08e2be612c
msgid "a guide to understanding the formats of data logger messages is `HERE <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/README.md>`__ and how the code for these messages is parsed and checked for inclusion in the documentation is `HERE <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/Tools/autotest/logger_metadata/README.md>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:17
#: 48500ef82b68419eb91c72266062c363
msgid "The Easy Way"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:19
#: 9ef3db28b00e433e91bbdb062d63e63c
msgid "Use `AP::logger().Write(...) <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/AP_Logger.h#L278>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:26
#: e4e2129853674fd3aa482d4cb06b6005
msgid "An example of the top function being used can be found in `Compass_learn.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Compass/Compass_learn.cpp#L99>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:40
#: 1bd3e8e0bff24ce6966c90083e63e5bd
msgid "the 1st argument is the message name.  This should be 4 characters or less and be unique"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:41
#: 94a8fb2c208743aaa82fb1fd2787615f
msgid "the 2nd argument is a comma separated list of up to 16 field names; with a limit of 64 characters in total"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:42
#: 6fdd0f7c5a464f4d9a78558bdf6a40c4
msgid "the 3rd argument is a format string (maximum of 16 characters) with each letter holding the format for the corresponding field.  The meaning of each letter can be found `here in AP_Logger/LogStructure.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L6>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:43
#: f390a11d1cf54aa79b87a2dc0e2b6725
msgid "the remaining arguments are the actual values that will be logged."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:45
#: 63011bdd20cd4c1e89b913e3bd2d6214
msgid "The 2nd Log_Write function is the same as the first except that it accepts two additional string arguments, `\"units\" <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L42>`__ and `\"mults\" <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L86>`__. Similar to the \"format\" argument, each character in these arguments specifies the `units <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L42>`__ (i.e. \"d\" for degrees) or `multiplier <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L86>`__ (i.e. \"2\" for \\*100, \"B\" for \\*0.01) for the following fields. These help the graphing tools scale the output correctly when displaying to the user."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:53
#: df0bff3b123f4656911e80e32e550e84
msgid "For example, below is a \"TEST\" log message which outputs the current system time and altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:64
#: 6d7f14da013a46bcb6880b169b20f242
msgid "the time has units of seconds (\"s\"), multiplier of \"F\" to indicate the value should be divided by 1 million and format of \"Q\" to indicate it is output as a 64 bit unsigned integer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:65
#: 0892cf0cf6eb4f1ab890a7200423bdde
msgid "the altitude has units of meters (\"m\"), multiplier of \"B\" to indicate the value should be divided by 100 (to convert from centimeters to meters) and format of \"f\" because the value is a float."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:68
#: c598198cae9948019e2b9373aea491da
msgid "The Harder Way"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:70
#: fa0b3343abb04ca9839070df4f1512d8
msgid "For commonly used messages, especially those which are output at a relatively high rate (50hz or more) a slightly more efficient logging method can be used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:72
#: b8b58ef29732425ead51542c63bbab45
msgid "decide if the logging will come from a library (i.e. the call to Log_Write will from somewhere within the `libraries directory <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/libraries>`__) or the vehicle code (i.e. from within `ArduCopter <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/ArduCopter>`__, `ArduPlane <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/tree/master/ArduPlane>`__, etc)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:75
#: 88fe77514e32452a8ea24988c455ccc4
msgid "add a new entry to the `vehicle's #define list or enum in defines.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/defines.h#L222>`__ or `AP_Logger/LogStructure.h's LogMessages enum <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L1566>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:76
#: bd106ab3d4da4f44b7389b1c001a4459
msgid "define a structure to hold the values to be logged in either the vehicle's `Log.cpp <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Log.cpp>`__ file or in `AP_Logger/LogStructure.h <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h>`__.  All log file messages should have time_us as their first field."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:87
#: 1672dea678b54835ab7b649611da018d
msgid "add the log message's name, `units <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L42>`__, `multiplier <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L86>`__ and `format <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L6>`__ strings into the `vehicle's LogStructure array <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/ArduCopter/Log.cpp#L454>`__ or `AP_Logger/LogStructure.h's LOG_EXTRA_STRUCTURES array <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/LogStructure.h#L1360>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:89
#: cd8e6d1d292d4ed18338429d32dfef2c
msgid "add a new method to the vehicle code or AP_Logger library called Write_<something-or-other> which fills in the structure and then calls `AP_Logger/WriteBlock() <https://github.com/ArduPilot/ardupilot/blob/master/libraries/AP_Logger/AP_Logger.h#L197>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/code-overview-adding-a-new-log-message.rst:103
#: db03cc341ee747418561a1df1dcfa003
msgid "call this new function from the :ref:`scheduler <code-overview-scheduling-your-new-code-to-run-intermittently>` or from some other place in the code at the moment you wish to log the values"
msgstr ""
